Thanks for the links. Something to pass the time on the bus to work.<br><blockquote class="uncited"><div>The way CG and LBFGS operate is to minimize the cost function without regard to the residual (velocity errors). The velocity errors are erratic through the iterations. The consequence of early termination is unstable stacking.</div></blockquote>Maybe Conjugate Residuals would be better suited? Again, I've never tried it, but it minimizes || A^(-1/2) (b-Ax)||_2 over the Krylov subspace at each step (Golub &amp; Van Loan, 10.4.3)...<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1158">Chris Elion</a> — Tue Jan 30, 2007 7:58 am</p><hr />
